{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '1640,1760p' src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'eligible\\\\?|py/call-kw|yang.call' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; rg --files test/yang/typescript | sort\"","aggregated_output":"(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.typescript.antlr.prelude/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n yang.typescript.antlr.prelude\n  \"The `js` runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md sections 3, 9, 10; the T1 plan's\n   section 6). JavaScript semantics for operators, coercion, equality,\n   strings, objects, functions and exceptions live here as guest code,\n   not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n\n   Value encoding:\n     undefined, null  :js/undefined, :js/null (and the never guest-visible\n                      :js/tdz of an uninitialized binding): never host nil\n     boolean          host true / false\n     number           float64 content (`data/float64`) at the producer, on\n                      every host (JS cannot tell 2 from 2.0 as a bare\n                      Number). Arithmetic unwraps with `data/float-value`,\n                      computes on bare host doubles and rewraps with\n                      `data/float64`. The prelude holds no integral float\n                      literal: 1 is written (data/float64 1)\n     bigint           the bare exact integer, through `integer/*`; a number\n                      and a bigint are told apart by content equality with\n                      the same value as float64 (`js/kind-of`)\n     string           {:js/str s} when the code units are well-formed\n                      UTF-16, {:js/units [u ...]} otherwise; `js/mk-str` is\n                      the one normalizing door, so strict equality of\n                      strings is host `=`\n     object           a cell holding {:js/type :object :proto <ref|:js/null>\n                      :props <om> :extensible? true}; the guest reference\n                      is the cell ref, identity is `=` on refs\n     function         a cell holding {:js/type :function :code\n                      (fn [this args] ..) :yang.call/entry\n                      (fn [invocation] ..) :this-mode :strict|:lexical\n                      :name s :length n :props <om> :proto ref}\n     property slot    {:value v :writable b :enumerable b :configurable b}\n     own-key map      `om`: {:index {key slot} :ints [..sorted..] :strs\n                      [..insertion..] :syms []}; guest-visible order is the\n                      vectors, never a host map's\n\n   Calling convention: source calls are (js/call f this args), with `args`\n   a vector built by `js/vconj`; `js/call` supplies one invocation record\n   to the shared entry. Constructors retain (js/construct F args), and a\n   function's private code is (fn [this args] ..).\n\n   Control flow is continuations: `js/throw`, `js/try`, `js/try-finally`\n   and `js/call-ec` copy the Python prelude's escape machinery with JS\n   payloads: `js/throw` takes any value, the handler stack lives in the one\n   record cell `js.rt/ctx` ({:handlers} only), and a flag cell tells a\n   first pass through a capture point from a re-entry.\n\n   Runtime state is allocated by `js/init!`, once per task, under\n   `js.rt/*` keys (`js.rt/state` is the literal :js/uninit until `js/init!`\n   flips it to :js/ready as its last write; a second call allocates\n   nothing): the context and out cells, the global object and the intrinsic\n   prototypes. The definitions are one list; `uast` is the bundled prelude\n   and `module-uast` the same list as the linker module `js`. The module\n   emitter strips only the namespace `js/`, so no definition is named like\n   a primitive (`js/get-prop`, not `js/get`), and no binder inside the\n   prelude is named like a definition.\n\n   Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`\n   (the cell module from yin.vm.module, the integer module from\n   yin.vm.integer, the rest from yin.vm.data).\"\n  #?(:cljs (:require-macros [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :refer [defquoted]]))\n  (:require\n    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\n    [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.core.call :as call]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n\n\n#?(:clj\n   (defmacro defquoted\n     \"`def` of the quoted data `form`. ClojureDart compiles quoted data to\n      straight-line Dart, which the Dart AOT compiler cannot take as one\n      initializer, so there the data is one EDN string read back at load.\"\n     [name doc form]\n     (if (find-ns 'cljd.compiler)\n       (list 'def name doc (list 'edn/read-string (pr-str (second form))))\n       (list 'def name doc form))))\n\n\n(def host-names\n  \"Module exports the prelude calls.\"\n  (into '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! data/count data/into data/subvec\n           data/number? data/nth data/str-concat data/str-length data/substring\n           data/str->code-points data/code-points->str data/float64\n           data/float-value data/content= data/str-unit-length data/str-unit-at\n           data/str-units data/units->str integer/add integer/sub integer/neg\n           integer/mul integer/compare integer/quot-rem integer/to-float\n           integer/compare-float integer/pow integer/shift-right\n           integer/shift-left integer/bit-and integer/bit-or integer/bit-xor\n           integer/bit-not integer/from-float integer/floor-div-mod\n           integer/format integer/parse integer/float-digits\n           integer/decimal->float}\n        call/host-names))\n\n\n(defquoted ^:private core-definitions\n  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n  '[;; ----------------------------------------------------------------- kinds\n    [js/cell? (fn [x] (= (get x :type) :cell-ref))]\n    [js/symbol?\n     (fn [x]\n       (if (js/cell? x) (= (get (cell/get x) :js/type) :symbol) false))]\n    [js/object? (fn [x] (if (js/cell? x) (not (js/symbol? x)) false))]\n    [js/make-symbol\n     (fn [description]\n       (cell/new (assoc (assoc {} :js/type :symbol) :description description)))]\n    [js/str?\n     (fn [x]\n       (if (nil? (get x :js/str)) (not (nil? (get x :js/units))) true))]\n    [js/pair (fn [a b] (conj (conj [] a) b))]\n    [js/vconj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n    [js/arg (fn [args i] (get args i :js/undefined))]\n    [js/kind-of\n     ;; undefined null boolean number bigint string function object. A\n     ;; number is float64 content, a bigint a bare exact integer: content\n     ;; equality with the same value as float64 tells them apart on every\n     ;; host (the JS carrier is not a host number at all)\n     (fn [x]\n       (if (= x :js/undefined)\n         :undefined\n         (if (= x :js/null)\n           :null\n           (if (= x true)\n             :boolean\n             (if (= x false)\n               :boolean\n               (if (data/number? x)\n                 (if (data/content= x (data/float64 x)) :number :bigint)\n                 (if (js/str? x)\n                   :string\n                   (if (js/cell? x)\n                     (if (= (get (cell/get x) :js/type) :function)\n                       :function\n                       (if (= (get (cell/get x) :js/type) :symbol)\n                         :symbol\n                         :object))\n                     :number))))))))]\n    [js/ty (fn [k] (if (= k :function) :object k))]\n    [js/prim-type?\n     (fn [t]\n       (if (= t :string)\n         true\n         (if (= t :number) true (if (= t :symbol) true (= t :bigint)))))]\n    [js/callable?\n     (fn [x]\n       (yang.call/eligible? x))]\n    [js/mknum (fn [x] (data/float64 x))]\n    [js/fval (fn [x] (data/float-value x))]\n    [js/nan-raw (fn [] (let [i (data/float-value ##Inf)] (- i i)))]\n    [js/nan (fn [] (data/float64 (js/nan-raw)))]\n    [js/habs (fn [x] (if (< x 0) (- 0 x) x))]\n    [js/finite? (fn [x] (< (js/habs x) (data/float-value ##Inf)))]\n    [js/zero-d? (fn [x] (= x (data/float-value 0)))]\n    [js/neg-zero-d?\n     (fn [x]\n       (if (js/zero-d? x)\n         (data/content= (data/float64 x)\n                        (data/float64 (* (data/float-value -1)\n                                         (data/float-value 0))))\n         false))]\n    [js/neg-zero\n     (fn []\n       (data/float64 (* (data/float-value -1) (data/float-value 0))))]\n    [js/int-result\n     ;; the `integer` module answers a limit breach as a reason\n     (fn [r]\n       (if (= r :yin.vm.integer/bit-limit)\n         (js/throw-range-error {:js/str \"Maximum BigInt size exceeded\"})\n         (if (= r :yin.vm.integer/digit-limit)\n           (js/throw-range-error {:js/str \"Maximum BigInt size exceeded\"})\n           r)))]\n\n    ;; --------------------------------------------------------------- strings\n    ;; A string is {:js/str host-string} when its code units are well-formed\n    ;; UTF-16 and {:js/units [u ...]} otherwise; `js/mk-str` is the one door\n    ;; that normalizes (it takes a vector of code units; a host string is\n    ;; well-formed and is wrapped as {:js/str s}), so strict equality is host `=`.\n    [js/mk-str\n     (fn [us]\n       (let [r (data/units->str us)]\n         (if (nil? (get r :yin.vm.data/refusal))\n           (assoc {} :js/str r)\n           (assoc {} :js/units us))))]\n    [js/units-of\n     (fn [s]\n       (if (nil? (get s :js/str))\n         (get s :js/units)\n         (data/str-units (get s :js/str))))]\n    [js/str-unit-length\n     (fn [s]\n       (if (nil? (get s :js/str))\n         (data/count (get s :js/units))\n         (data/str-unit-length (get s :js/str))))]\n    [js/str-unit-at\n     (fn [s i]\n       (if (nil? (get s :js/str))\n         (get (get s :js/units) i)\n         (data/str-unit-at (get s :js/str) i)))]\n    [js/str-concat\n     (fn [a b]\n       (if (nil? (get a :js/str))\n         (js/mk-str (data/into (get a :js/units) (js/units-of b)))\n         (if (nil? (get b :js/str))\n           (js/mk-str (data/into (js/units-of a) (get b :js/units)))\n           (assoc {} :js/str (data/str-concat (get a :js/str) (get b :js/str))))))]\n    [js/str-slice\n     ;; the units [from, to) of s, 0 <= from <= to <= length\n     (fn [s from to]\n       (js/mk-str (data/subvec (js/units-of s) from to)))]\n    [js/units-compare\n     (fn [x y i]\n       (let [nx (data/count x)\n             ny (data/count y)]\n         (if (if (<= nx i) true (<= ny i))\n           (if (< nx ny) -1 (if (> nx ny) 1 0))\n           (let [p (get x i)\n                 q (get y i)]\n             (if (< p q) -1 (if (> p q) 1 (js/units-compare x y (+ i 1))))))))]\n    [js/str-compare\n     ;; -1, 0 or 1 by UTF-16 code unit, as the relational operators order\n     (fn [a b]\n       (if (= a b) 0 (js/units-compare (js/units-of a) (js/units-of b) 0)))]\n    [js/units-match?\n     (fn [xs ys i j]\n       (if (<= (data/count ys) j)\n         true\n         (if (= (get xs (+ i j)) (get ys j))\n           (js/units-match? xs ys i (+ j 1))\n           false)))]\n    [js/units-index\n     (fn [xs ys i]\n       (if (< (- (data/count xs) (data/count ys)) i)\n         -1\n         (if (js/units-match? xs ys i 0) i (js/units-index xs ys (+ i 1)))))]\n\n    ;; ---------------------------------------------------- number to string\n    [js/zeros\n     (fn [n acc]\n    (if cname\n      (bind-cells [[cname tdz]] inner)\n      inner)))\n\n\n(defn- lower-primary\n  [ctx k]\n  (cond\n    (p/rule? k \"arrayLiteral\") (lower-array ctx k)\n    (p/rule? k \"objectLiteral\") (lower-object ctx k)\n    (p/token? k \"this\") (lower-this-expr ctx)\n    (p/rule? k \"literal\") (lower-literal ctx k)\n    (p/rule? k \"identifierName\")\n    (let [t (text-of ctx k)]\n      (case t\n        \"null\" (u/lit :js/null)\n        \"true\" (u/lit true)\n        \"false\" (u/lit false)\n        (read-name ctx t)))\n    (p/rule? k \"anonymousFunction\") (function-node ctx k nil)\n    :else (default-arm k)))\n\n\n(defn- lower-expr\n  \"The node of `singleExpression` `n`.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (let [ks (kids ctx n)\n        c (count ks)\n        k0 (first ks)\n        k1 (when (< 1 c) (second ks))]\n    (cond\n      (= c 1) (lower-primary ctx k0)\n      (p/token? k0 \"class\") (lower-class ctx n nil)\n      (p/rule? k0 \"typeArguments\") (refuse! n \"type syntax\" :T8)\n      (and (= c 3) (p/token? k0 \"(\")) (lower-seq ctx k1)\n      (and (p/token? k0 \"new\") (= c 3) (p/token? k1 \".\"))\n      (nt-node ctx)\n      (and (= c 3) (p/rule? k0 \"privateIdentifier\") (p/token? k1 \"in\"))\n      (app* 'js/priv-has\n            (lower-expr ctx (nth ks 2))\n            (u/v (private-sym ctx k0 (str \"#\" (text-of ctx (second (kids ctx k0)))))))\n      (p/token? k0 \"new\") (lower-new ctx n)\n      (and (= c 2) (p/token? k0)) (lower-prefix ctx n (:text k0) k1)\n      (and (= c 2) (p/rule? k1 \"arguments\")) (lower-call ctx n)\n      (and (= c 3) (p/rule? k1 \"typeArguments\")) (refuse! n \"type syntax\" :T8)\n      (and (= c 2) (p/rule? k1 \"templateStringLiteral\"))\n      (refuse! n \"tagged template\" :T5)\n      (and (= c 2) (p/token? k1 \"!\")) (refuse! n \"type syntax\" :T8)\n      (and (= c 2) (p/token? k1))\n      (lower-update ctx n k0 (:text k1) false)\n      (and (= c 3) (or (p/token? k1 \"as\") (p/token? k1 \"satisfies\")))\n      (refuse! n \"type syntax\" :T8)\n      (and (= c 3) (p/token? k1 \"=\")) (lower-assign ctx n k0 \"=\" (nth ks 2))\n      (and (= c 3) (p/rule? k1 \"assignmentOperator\"))\n      (lower-assign ctx n k0 (text-of ctx k1) (nth ks 2))\n      (member-expression? ctx n) (lower-member-read ctx n)\n      (and (= c 5) (p/token? k1 \"?\") (p/token? (nth ks 3) \":\"))\n      (u/if-node (truthy (lower-expr ctx k0))\n                 (lower-expr ctx (nth ks 2))\n                 (lower-expr ctx (nth ks 4)))\n      (and (<= 3 c)\n           (p/rule? k0 \"singleExpression\")\n           (p/rule? (peek ks) \"singleExpression\")\n           (every? p/token? (butlast (rest ks))))\n      (lower-binary ctx n ks)\n      :else (default-arm n))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-named\n  \"`lower-expr` with function-name hint `nm` for an anonymous function.\"\n  [ctx n nm]\n  (let [ks (kids ctx n)]\n    (cond\n      (and (= 1 (count ks)) (p/rule? (first ks) \"anonymousFunction\"))\n      (let [f (first (kids ctx (first ks)))]\n        (if (p/rule? f \"functionDeclaration\")\n          (lower-expr ctx n)\n          (function-node ctx (first ks) nm)))\n      (and (p/token? (first ks) \"class\")\n           (nil? (first (rules ctx n \"identifier\"))))\n      (lower-class ctx n nm)\n      :else (lower-expr ctx n))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-seq\n  \"The node of an `expressionSequence`: comma sequencing.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (u/seq-nodes (mapv #(lower-expr ctx %) (rules ctx n \"singleExpression\"))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Statements\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(declare lower-stmt lower-block)\n\n\n(defn statements-of\n  \"The `statement` nodes below a program, function body, block or case\n   clause.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (let [holder (or (first (rules ctx n \"sourceElements\"))\n                   (first (rules ctx n \"statementList\")))]\n    (if holder\n      (mapv (fn [el]\n              (if (p/rule? el \"sourceElement\")\n                (do (when (token-kid ctx el \"export\")\n                      (refuse! el \"module syntax\" :T7))\n                    (first (rules ctx el \"statement\")))\n                el))\n            (rule-kids ctx holder))\n      [])))\n\n\n(defn- function-statement?\n  [ctx st]\n  (p/rule? (first (rule-kids ctx st)) \"functionDeclaration\"))\n\n\n(defn- hoisted-init\n  [ctx st]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:21:     with keywords, `(py/call-kw f [args] [[name value] ...])`; the callee\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1112:  \"`(py/call f args)`, or `(py/call-kw f args kwargs)` when the call\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:1116:    (app* 'py/call-kw f args kwargs)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:64:   laid out as the parameters are written. `py/call-kw` (and `py/call`,\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:887:       (let [callee (get invocation :yang.call/callee :py/missing)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:888:             positional (get invocation :yang.call/positional :py/missing)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:889:             named (get invocation :yang.call/named :py/missing)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:890:             raise-exit (get invocation :yang.call/raise :py/missing)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:891:             binding-profile (get invocation :yang.call/binding-profile :py/missing)]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:897:           (raise-exit {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/invalid-invocation})\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:899:             (raise-exit (assoc {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding}\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:900:                                :yang.call/binding-profile binding-profile))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:909:                   (raise-exit (assoc {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown}\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:910:                                      :yang.call/value e)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:922:           (do (cell/set! f (assoc (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1030:    [py/call (fn [f args] (py/call-kw f args []))]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1031:    [py/call-kw\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1034:         (py/call-kw (get f :fn) (data/into (py/vconj [] (get f :self)) args) kwargs)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:1061:               (py/call-kw init (d