{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show efc99cc4 --stat; git show efc99cc4 -- test/yang/python/antlr/source_call_test.clj; rg -n 'export|lower-program|lower-module|namespace' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/*publication* test/yang/php/antlr/*linked*; cat deps.edn | tail -130; cat shadow-cljs.edn | head -110; rg --files -g AGENTS.md src test\"","aggregated_output":"commit efc99cc45b78b6a5fd5da9a52c993e8807c2d966\nMerge: 63674368 13ba4a2f\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\nDate:   Sat Oct 31 02:36:25 2026 +0700\n\n    Merge python-s3-wiring: Python source calls route through the shared yang.call convention (S3 of the 8.10 adoption)\n    \n    The :call lowering resolves admitted callables through the shared\n    convention (yang.call/eligible? -> entry -> invoke) with Python\n    semantics preserved for Python callees; both emitters carry the yang.call\n    runtime; the linked path requires it before py (the wrapper fix plus\n    py's module-tree require — the root cause of the linked-import reds);\n    ordinary and SCC source modules require and pin it when their bodies\n    reference the convention. The closure ledgers and per-lane totals\n    include the shared runtime; the Python and TypeScript float-address\n    pins re-minted for the emission drift; the entry fixture combines the\n    binder fixtures with the source-call-helper and cross-frontend identity\n    tests.\n    \n    Kimi k3.1-pro gate: READY (session_664f487a-5b62-4f41-b7cd-8cfddfcb5f18)\n    — the routing implements 8.10.4 without language-pair dispatch, the\n    marks rule holds, the shared surfaces ruled sound. Evidence at 13ba4a2f\n    on shiva: main-test 49/412/0 (the J6e adapter composed), import-test\n    50/436/0 unfiltered (slow bodies), float-address Python 12/105/0 and TS\n    5/20/0, call-entry 3/12/0, call-test 4/15/0, publication 10/85/0,\n    gate-test 14/178/0, kondo 0/0, cljstyle clean, 