t, once each, before the\n            outer handler\"\n    (doseq [[k result]\n            (run-with-prelude\n              prelude/uast\n              '(let [log (cell/new [])]\n                 (js/vconj\n                   (js/vconj\n                     []\n                     (js/try (fn []\n                               (js/try-finally\n                                 (fn []\n                                   (js/try-finally\n                                     (fn [] (js/throw 1))\n                                     (fn [x] (cell/set! log (js/vconj (cell/get log) :a)))))\n                                 (fn [x] (cell/set! log (js/vconj (cell/get log) :b)))))\n                             (fn [e] e)))\n                   (cell/get log))))]\n      (testing (str k)\n        (is (= [1 [:a :b]] (if (vector? result) result [:thrown result])))))))\n\nbb.edn:233:   ;; The Node lanes (test:cljs and its variants) depend on this task, so the\nbb.edn:252:   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\nbb.edn:272:  {:doc \"Babashka-only, no natives: scan deps.edn :paths + :cljs :extra-paths for .cljc/.cljs namespaces outside test/ matching shadow-cljs.edn :test :ns-regexp (default -test$); fail before Node discovery can load JVM-only code. Rename the ns or guard it with reader conditionals. Self-test: bb src/dev/check_node_discovery_test.clj\"\nbb.edn:275:  test:cljs {:doc \"Node tests, fast: dao.test-slow guarded bodies print SKIP; needs the Node REPL build\"\nbb.edn:288:  test:all:cljs {:doc \"Every Node test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\nbb.edn:304:  test:slow:cljs {:doc \"Node: only namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\nbb.edn:321:             :depends [test:slow:clj test:slow:cljs test:slow:cljd]}\nbb.edn:324:            :depends [test:all:clj test:all:cljs test:all:cljd]}\nbb.edn:327:        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}\nbb.edn:358:  test:changed:cljs {:doc \"Node lane of test:changed\"\nbb.edn:402:  test:sub:cljs {:doc \"Node lane of test:sub: bb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>... [--slow]\"\nsrc/dev/affected.clj:152:  #\"^(?:src/(?:clj|cljc|cljs|cljd|dev)/|test/)(.+)\\.(?:clj|cljc|cljs|cljd)$\")\nsrc/dev/affected.clj:167:    (mapv #(str \"test/\" rel \"_test.\" %) [\"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljs\" \"cljd\"])))\nsrc/dev/affected.clj:606:               (fs/glob \"test\" \"**.{clj,cljc,cljs,cljd}\"))\n---\ndescription: High-Throughput Subagent Worker role definition for datom.world\n---\n\n# ROLE: High-Throughput Subagent Worker\n\n## Domain Scope\n\n- Bounded searches and repository inventories\n- Small, explicitly scoped source or documentation edits\n- Mechanical synchronization across known file sets\n- Focused lint, formatting, and test execution when tools are enabled\n- Evidence collection for an orchestrator or domain engineer\n\nThis role owns no permanent file list. Each task must provide explicit file\nauthority, acceptance criteria, and permitted checks.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Stay Bounded**: Work only within named files and acceptance criteria.\n2. **Preserve User Work**: Leave unrelated tracked and untracked changes untouched.\n3. **Report Evidence**: Distinguish observed repository state from inference.\n4. **Verify Claims**: Run only the requested checks and report exact outcomes.\n5. **Escalate Decisions**: Return architectural ambiguity to the orchestrator instead of expanding scope.\n\n## Delegation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: High-Throughput Subagent Worker\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nPerform <search/edit/documentation/check-task> in <repository-root>.\n\nAuthorized files:\n- <path-1>\n- <path-2>\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- <criterion-1>\n- <criterion-2>\n\nPreserve unrelated changes. Do not broaden file scope or make architectural\ndecisions. For implementation work, edit the authorized files and run\n<focused-check-command>. For read-only work, do not edit files.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nThen report files inspected or changed, evidence found, exact check outcomes,\nscope expansion requests, and incomplete work. Do not claim actions that did\nnot occur.\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
