{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.git/hooks/pre-commit; rg -n '11|call|S11' docs/design/yang.typescript.md | tail -25; sed -n '294,336p' test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc; wc -l test/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call*; tail -12 /tmp/ts-s11-source-current.log\"","aggregated_output":"#!/bin/sh\n# Pre-commit hook: format only staged Clojure files.\n# Works per-file to avoid stash conflicts with unstaged changes.\n\n# 0. Refuse to commit collab/ IN-FLIGHT artifacts. Flat files directly under\n#    collab/ are the untracked in-flight workspace: append-only, never staged\n#    or committed, and never ignored/excluded (docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md,\n#    artifact protocol). Owner-approved 2026-09-30. Since the 2026-10-31 owner\n#    ruling, collab/ is also the archive root: its topic SUBFOLDERS\n#    (collab/yang-python/ etc.) are version-controlled and committable — only\n#    single-segment collab/<file> paths are refused. Deletions are always\n#    allowed so tracked files can be untracked with `git rm --cached`.\nCOLLAB=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR -- collab/ | grep -E '^collab/[^/]+$' || true)\nif [ -n \"$COLLAB\" ]; then\n    echo \"pre-commit: refusing to commit in-flight collab/ artifacts (flat collab/<file> paths are never committed; topic subfolders are allowed):\" >&2\n    echo \"$COLLAB\" | sed 's/^/  /' >&2\n    echo \"Unstage them with: git restore --staged -- <paths>\" >&2\n    exit 1\nfi\n\n# 1. Get staged .clj* files (Added, Copied, Modified only)\nSTAGED=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM | grep '\\.clj' || true)\n\nif [ -z \"$STAGED\" ]; then\n    exit 0\nfi\n\necho \"Running formatters on staged files...\"\n\nTMPDIR=$(mktemp -d)\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"' EXIT\n\nfor file in $STAGED; do\n    mkdir -p \"$TMPDIR/$(dirname \"$file\")\"\n\n    # Save working tree version (may have unstaged changes)\n    cp \"$file\" \"$TMPDIR/worktree_$( echo \"$file\" | tr '/' '_' )\"\n\n    # Extract staged content to work on\n    git show \":$file\" > \"$file\"\n\n    # Save staged content before formatting\n    cp \"$file\" \"$TMPDIR/staged_$( echo \"$file\" | tr '/' '_' )\"\n\n    # Format the staged content in place.\n    # cljstyle only, matching src/dev/tasks.clj fix-all. zprint was removed:\n    # with no .zprintrc it ran on its own defaults, rewrote ~546 lines of an\n    # already-canonical file, and cljstyle fix then restored it exactly -- a\n    # net no-op that churned every staged file on every commit. It was also a\n    # latent hazard: anything zprint changes that cljstyle has no rule to\n    # normalise back would be silently committed (e.g. reader-conditional\n    # branch order, whose cljstyle :namespaces rule is disabled project-wide).\n    mise exec -- cljstyle fix \"$file\" 2>/dev/null\n\n    # Re-stage the formatted version\n    git add \"$file\"\n\n    # Save formatted version\n    cp \"$file\" \"$TMPDIR/formatted_$( echo \"$file\" | tr '/' '_' )\"\n\n    # Restore working tree: if the file had no unstaged changes\n    # (worktree == staged), use the formatted version. Otherwise\n    # restore the original worktree to preserve unstaged edits.\n    KEY=$( echo \"$file\" | tr '/' '_' )\n    if diff -q \"$TMPDIR/worktree_$KEY\" \"$TMPDIR/staged_$KEY\" > /dev/null 2>&1; then\n        cp \"$TMPDIR/formatted_$KEY\" \"$file\"\n    else\n        cp \"$TMPDIR/worktree_$KEY\" \"$file\"\n    fi\ndone\n\necho \"Formatting complete.\"\nexit 0\n981:### 11.4 Evaluate (commit per strongly connected component)\n1005:### 11.5 The operation matrix\n1063:### 11.6 Dynamic import, the job rule and top-level await\n1072:meanwhile. Consequences: a module that calls `import(\"./self\")` and then\n1080:section 11.4 is complete.\n1092:### 11.7 Publication\n1106:### 11.8 Refused resolution\n1115:### 11.9 The REPL binding\n1260:- **Safepoints** (`yang.antlr.md` 8.5.2): `:loop` and `:call` marks only, with\n1261:  hook prelude `jssp` providing `jssp/loop` and `jssp/call`, which poll a\n1265:  Maximum call stack size exceeded` is available as a profile-pinned depth\n1275:  the dynamic-import narrowing of section 11.6.\n1290:11).\n1305:  per-iteration `let`, closures in loops); `this` (bare calls, methods,\n1306:  arrows, bound functions, `call`/`apply`); prototypes (shadowing, `in`,\n1338:|       | `safepoint.cljc` call it         |                                   |\n1341:|       | lowering and stage helpers       | `packet.cljc` emits the caller's  |\n1426:|       | module records, link and SCC     | hoisted-function call before the  |\n1514:guest call sites are deferred to a checker slice outside both frontends: every\n1515:guest call lowers to `js/call f this args`, so no guest binder is the operator\n1519:known-gaps ledger row is \"guest-aware call meeting points for the checker\",\n1553:`frame`, `raise`, `unwind-to`, `try`, `try-finally`, `call-ec`; the generator\n1573:`await`; CommonJS and ambient resolution (section 11.8).\n1579:  (section 11.6);\n1630:11. (A12.11) Binder tables as publication datoms beside the manifest\n  (let [bundled (lower/lower-packet var-x)\n        linked (lower/lower-packet var-x {:prelude :linked})]\n    (is (not= bundled linked))\n    (is (< (count (pr-str linked)) (count (pr-str bundled)))\n        \"the linked program carries no prelude tree\")\n    (is (some #(= (u/lit 'js) %) (nodes linked)) \"it requires the module js\")\n    (is (some #(and (map? %) (= (u/v 'js/init!) (:operator %))) (nodes linked))\n        \"and allocates the task's state\")\n    (is (some #(and (map? %) (= (u/v 'js/run-main) (:operator %)))\n              (nodes bundled)))))\n\n\n(deftest linked-source-requires-convention-before-js-test\n  (doseq [ast [(lower/lower-packet var-x {:prelude :linked})\n               (lower/lower-units [var-x] {:prelude :linked})\n               (lower/lower-units [] {:prelude :linked})]]\n    (let [forms (loop [node ast\n                       suffix ()]\n                  (if (= [u/discard] (get-in node [:operator :params]))\n                    (recur (first (:operands node))\n                           (cons (get-in node [:operator :body]) suffix))\n                    (cons node suffix)))\n          requires (take 2 forms)]\n      (is (every? #(= (u/v 'require) (:operator %)) requires))\n      (is (= '[yang.call js]\n             (mapv #(get-in % [:operands 0 :value]) requires))))))\n\n\n(deftest bundled-program-depth-test\n  ;; A linear prelude sequence reached 976 levels with 481 definitions:\n  ;; `pr-str` could overflow even though the tree contained no cycle.\n  ;; Leave room for the runtime bodies, but catch that sequencing growth\n  ;; independently of the JVM printer's stack size and JIT warmup.\n  (is (< (tree-depth (lower/lower-packet var-x)) 512)))\n\n\n(deftest transform-routes-programs-and-diagnostics-test\n  (let [[_ [[port envelope]]] (lower/lower-transform {} var-x)]\n    (is (= :program port))\n    (is (= {:yin/source-medium lower/program-medium,\n            :yin/batch-token [:hand 0],\n            :yin/batch [(lower/lower-packet var-x)],\n            :yin/root 0}\n     438 test/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call_fixtures.cljc\n      14 test/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call_parser_test.clj\n     101 test/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call_test.cljc\n     553 total\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yang.typescript.antlr.source-call-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
