ppers into with-runtime, preserving the unconditional yang.call-before-js sequence. A portable test covers single-unit, multi-unit, and empty multi-unit programs.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793620000000-engineer-ts-yangcall-routing.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:19:- Real-source tests: separately lower PHP source; publish an ordinary module exporting its unchanged body and the PHP runtime; run the donor; resolve functions with the published php/resolve-fn export; project those same cells with js/define-global!. TS source body is lowered unchanged. Bundled runs use the same namespace projection. No AST walks, call-node rewriting, foreign :code extraction, replacement function cells, or language-pair call wrappers.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793620000000-engineer-ts-yangcall-routing.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:22:- Portable CST fixtures include the original source strings. JVM parser checks prove each recorded CST form equals the parser output. Node/Dart can lower those same source-derived forms without a parser.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793620000000-engineer-ts-yangcall-routing.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:29:PHP routing/admission must recognize common entries before its local kind conversion and preserve its local string/Closure resolution. PHP's published runtime currently has no yang.call dependency, so a proper helper-based fix may also need the PHP module's shared-runtime dependency wiring. That work is outside the named TS implementation files; no test-local workaround has been inserted. Full §8.10 conformance is not claimed.\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793620000000-engineer-ts-yangcall-routing.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:33:Pending final targeted JVM/Node results; see /tmp/ts-s11-verify-summary.txt, /tmp/ts-s11-source-current.log, /tmp/ts-s11-node.log and /tmp/ts-s11-kondo.log. Final outcomes will be appended here before handoff.\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n[:test] Compiling ...\n========= Running Tests =